note: Boolean literals
a is True
b is False

output is a
output is b

note: not
output is not True
output is not False

note: and
output is True and True
output is True and False
output is False and True
output is False and False

note: or
output is True or True
output is True or False
output is False or True
output is False or False

note: precedence
output is True or False and False
output is False or True and True

note: comparisons
output is 10 > 5
output is 10 < 5
output is 10 >= 10
output is 10 <= 10
output is 10 == 10
output is 10 != 5

note: boolean variables in conditions
x = 10
if x > 5 and x < 20
then output is "condition works"
